---
description: Enforce zero-egress MCP security with SIP-1
alwaysApply: false
globs: "**/{.mcp.json,mcp.json,config.toml,*.sql,*.env*}"
---

# SHULIAK SIP-1 Local Security Rules

- Pin every npm MCP server to an exact version (@x.y.z).
- Never hardcode credentials or DSNs; use ${env:VAR_NAME}.
- Run npx -y @shuliak-corp/sip1-mcp@3.1.0 audit before
  committing any MCP client configuration.
- Before reading financial, legal, or clinical files
  (.docx, .xlsx, .pdf, HL7, FHIR), use
  sip_read_protected_file for in-RAM NIST FF1 scrubbing.
- Validate destructive SQL or shell commands with
  sip_classify_action_guard before execution.
